{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianShearIntegral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianShearIntegral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Gaussian.GaussianIntegral","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Pi"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.integral_vdv_step4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.integral_vdv_step4","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianShearIntegral.lean#L102-L139","doc":"**The Step-4 Gaussian: `2^{−n/2}·(2/A)^{1/2}`**, for every `n` and every\ncomplex `A` with `Re A > 0`.\n\nStated as the iterated integral (`v` first, then `u`) — see the file header on\nwhat that does and does not claim.  Note there is no rank restriction and no\n`erfc`: with the signs of the Taylor expansion restored, the transverse\nintegrals are complete Gaussians and the whole thing is elementary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.integral_cexp_neg_pi_mul_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.integral_cexp_neg_pi_mul_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianShearIntegral.lean#L83-L100","doc":"**`∫_ℝ e^{−πAu²/2} du = (2/A)^{1/2}`** for any complex `A` with `Re A > 0`.\n\n`Re A = c+d ≥ 1` on the Whitehead chains, so the hypothesis is never binding\nthere; it is exactly the condition that makes the Gaussian converge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.integral_cexp_two_pi_sq_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.integral_cexp_two_pi_sq_shift","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianShearIntegral.lean#L55-L81","doc":"**`∫_ℝ e^{−2π(v+s)²} dv = 2^{−1/2}`**, for every real shift `s`.\n\nThe complete Gaussian at covariance `2π` is `2^{−1/2}` and translation does not\nmove it.  Independence of `s` is the structural fact behind the `v`-integrals in\nStep 4: it is why the `n` transverse directions contribute a bare `2^{−n/2}` and\nleave the `u`-integral untouched. ","signatureChunk":0}]}